# [O-29] pcrec-bench 2026-09-16: the SUPPRESSED-ORDER CONTROL. A `tag`
# line placed AFTER a block's `provenance` sub-block (rather than before,
# or absent) was observed by the bench to hide the drop, and this pins
# why: `tag` is an ordinary CONTENT line, so its own arrival closes the
# still-open provenance frame through the dedent-pop while loop — the
# path that has always called `RXT_CLOSE_FRAME` correctly, both before
# and after the O-29 fix. Nothing about this shape ever needed fixing;
# it is the control that proves the fix did not change what already
# worked. Both blocks below end `provenance` ... `tag` ... <blank line>,
# so the blank line closes nothing (the frame is already closed by the
# time it arrives).
pattern p1 a
provenance
  source authored
  retrieved 2026-09-16
  license MIT
  fidelity verbatim
tag t1

pattern p2 b
provenance
  source authored
  retrieved 2026-09-16
  license MIT
  fidelity verbatim
tag t2
